WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.238
Aisha runs circulation at the library, and central is replacing the checkout system in six weeks.

2
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:14.567
Her team has heard the rumor, and two of them have already said, here we go again.

3
00:00:14.617 --> 00:00:18.813
Job three, make things better, is not a reorganization.

4
00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:25.606
It is four small habits, and Aisha uses all of them before the announcement email lands.

5
00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:32.862
Explain the why: at Thursday’s staff meeting, in her own words, before Tuesday’s campus email.

6
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:37.416
The old system loses holds at the handoff; this fixes that.

7
00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:42.511
A staffer asks a hard question; Aisha writes it down to take back.

8
00:00:42.561 --> 00:00:47.374
Describe where you are going: two sentences from the mezzanine,

9
00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:52.391
what the desk will be able to do next year that it cannot do now.

10
00:00:52.441 --> 00:01:00.033
Let people try: a young staffer wants to run the carts a new way; try it for two weeks and show me.

11
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:08.370
Look back: after move-in weekend, ten minutes around a table, three sticky notes, what worked, what did not,

12
00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.770
what changes. The team still did not love the new system.

13
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:18.328
But they heard the why from Aisha first, their questions went somewhere,

14
00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.801
and two of them volunteered to test it early.

15
00:01:21.851 --> 00:01:30.215
Vanderbilt is asking every team to move faster and improve, and that happens here, in small ways, every week.

16
00:01:30.265 --> 00:01:33.380
This week: hold one ten-minute look-back.

